\[\frac{\sqrt{3}}{4} \cdot 12^2 = 36 \sqrt{3}.\]Thus, the area of the right part of the shaded region is $24\pi - 36\sqrt{3},$ so the area of the entire shaded region is $$2(24\pi-36\sqrt{3})=\boxed{48\pi-72\sqrt{3}}.$$

